{"name":"Inuit Ice","hex":"#c2bdc2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inuit","blocks":[{"text":"Inuit are a group of culturally and historically similar Indigenous peoples traditionally inhabiting the Arctic and Subarctic regions of North America and Russia, including Greenland, Labrador, Quebec, Nunavut, the Northwest Territories, Yukon (traditionally), and Alaska. The Inuit languages are part of the Eskaleut languages, also known as Inuit-Yupik-Unangan and as Eskimo–Aleut."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Distribution_of_Inuit_in_Canada_%282021%29.svg/330px-Distribution_of_Inuit_in_Canada_%282021%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuit","wikidata":"Q189975"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/500px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/1280px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/500px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A European ship coming into contact with Inuit in the ice of Hudson Bay in 1697","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHistoire_de_l'Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_(1753)_(14577039230).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Zentralbibliothek_Z%C3%BCrich_-_Merckliche_Beschreibung_sampt_eygenlicher_Abbildung_eynes_frembden_unbekanten_Volcks_-_000003625_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Zentralbibliothek_Z%C3%BCrich_-_Merckliche_Beschreibung_sampt_eygenlicher_Abbildung_eynes_frembden_unbekanten_Volcks_-_000003625_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Zentralbibliothek_Z%C3%BCrich_-_Merckliche_Beschreibung_sampt_eygenlicher_Abbildung_eynes_frembden_unbekanten_Volcks_-_000003625_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Zentralbibliothek_Z%C3%BCrich_-_Merckliche_Beschreibung_sampt_eygenlicher_Abbildung_eynes_frembden_un